{
  "id": "u01-l03",
  "unit": "u01-basics",
  "title": "What's your name?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Adding **-র** (*-r*) makes 'my / your': আমি → **আমার** (*amar*, my), তুমি → **তোমার** (*tomar*), আপনি → **আপনার** (*apnar*). Match the 'your' to the 'you' you would use with that person.\n\nQuestion words stay where the answer goes: **আপনার নাম কী?** is literally 'Your name what?' and the answer is **আমার নাম রাফি** 'My name (is) Rafi'.\n\nSpelling note: **কী** (long ী) means 'what'; **কি** (short ি) is the yes/no question marker you'll meet in Unit 2. They sound the same.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "nam",
      "bn": "নাম",
      "tr": "nam",
      "en": "name"
    },
    {
      "id": "ki-what",
      "bn": "কী",
      "tr": "ki",
      "en": "what",
      "notes": "Spelled with long ী to distinguish it from the yes/no particle কি. Older texts may write কি for both."
    },
    {
      "id": "amar",
      "bn": "আমার",
      "tr": "amar",
      "en": "my"
    },
    {
      "id": "apnar",
      "bn": "আপনার",
